# SUPPLIED stimulus for the whole PicoRV32 unit.
# Input ordinals (picorv32_io.json): 2 mem_rdata, 3 mem_ready, 8 resetn.
# Output ordinal 8 is mem_valid.
#
# `react 3 8` wires mem_ready to the PREVIOUS cycle's mem_valid, which is the
# zero-latency memory handshake the core actually needs -- holding mem_ready
# high unconditionally acknowledges transactions the core never started.
# mem_rdata is held at `addi x1, x0, 1` (0x00100093), so every fetch retires an
# instruction that WRITES the 32x32 register file -- the aw5/dw32 memory this
# certificate declares.
stim v1
in 0 1 0
in 1 32 0
in 2 32 1048723
in 4 32 0
in 5 1 0
in 6 1 0
in 7 1 0
in 8 1 1
react 3 8
